  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616796",
      "title": "Extracting Dynamic Parameter Values",
      "sourceHash": "e33668d3afb957ed8631757887b3b7700d8d98ec9029b4095280f4f7b9108814",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.54,
          "en": "To extract the concrete value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.54,
          "end": 7.66,
          "en": "entered in the URL when this page is loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.66,
          "end": 10.78,
          "en": "Next.js gives us a special hook which we can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.78,
          "end": 12.13,
          "en": "A special react hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.13,
          "end": 14.8,
          "en": "which we can use in functional components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.8,
          "end": 18.25,
          "en": "It also has an alternative for a class-based components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.25,
          "end": 21.7,
          "en": "a higher order component you can wrap around your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.7,
          "end": 24.97,
          "en": "and I do discuss this in my full Next.js course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.97,
          "end": 27.01,
          "en": "but we can ignore that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.01,
          "end": 30.64,
          "en": "Here, instead we import from next to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.64,
          "end": 32.95,
          "en": "from next/router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.95,
          "end": 35.56,
          "en": "which is a sub package of the next package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.56,
          "end": 39.37,
          "en": "which exposes routing specific functionality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.37,
          "end": 41.91,
          "en": "And here we got the youth router hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.91,
          "end": 45.92,
          "en": "It's a regular react hook, just not one built into react",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.92,
          "end": 48.703,
          "en": "but accustomed hook built by the next team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.33,
          "end": 51.95,
          "en": "And we can now call this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.95,
          "end": 56.05,
          "en": "instead of the detailed page, simply like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.05,
          "end": 59.06,
          "en": "If we do that, we get access to a router object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.06,
          "end": 61.07,
          "en": "and on that router object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.07,
          "end": 63.5,
          "en": "we then got certain pieces of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.5,
          "end": 66.43,
          "en": "and certain methods which we can call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.43,
          "end": 70.25,
          "en": "Now, for example, we get methods for programmatic navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.25,
          "end": 73.58,
          "en": "but we don't need this here so we can ignore this for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.58,
          "end": 78.4,
          "en": "but we also get access to devalues encoded in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.4,
          "end": 82.463,
          "en": "so, to deconcrete values of these dynamic path segments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.48,
          "end": 86.38,
          "en": "And getting access is easy on this router object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.38,
          "end": 89.15,
          "en": "we've got this query property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.15,
          "end": 91.55,
          "en": "which gives us access to a nested object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.55,
          "end": 96.55,
          "en": "and on that query object we then have the identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.58,
          "end": 99.22,
          "en": "which we chose between the square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.22,
          "end": 100.88,
          "en": "as a property name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.88,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "So, in my case newsId because that's what I entered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.2,
          "en": "as a file name between the square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.2,
          "end": 111.47999999999999,
          "en": "And that will then hold the concrete value in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 115.9,
          "en": "for this dynamic segment for which this page was visited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.9,
          "end": 118.07,
          "en": "So, if we now just console log this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.07,
          "end": 120.163,
          "en": "for the moment to see what's in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.03,
          "end": 125.29,
          "en": "If I save that and go back and open the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.29,
          "end": 129.56,
          "en": "if we reload we see undefined first and then something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.56,
          "end": 131.14,
          "en": "Now, we see tool logs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.14,
          "end": 133.66,
          "en": "because that's how use router works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.66,
          "end": 136.67000000000002,
          "en": "It runs immediately when the pages first rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.67000000000002,
          "end": 140.77,
          "en": "and at this point it doesn't yet know what's in the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.77,
          "end": 142.73,
          "en": "but then once we have that information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.73,
          "end": 146.81,
          "en": "the component renders again and we got that concrete value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.81,
          "end": 149.57,
          "en": "that is just how that hook works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.57,
          "end": 152.3,
          "en": "So, the second time it executes the second time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.3,
          "end": 155.74,
          "en": "this component is evaluated we got something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.74,
          "end": 160.61,
          "en": "which is to concrete URL value I entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.61,
          "end": 164.18,
          "en": "And if I have this-course-is-great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.18,
          "end": 167.36,
          "en": "then we would see this here being locked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.36,
          "end": 168.88,
          "en": "And that's how we can get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.88,
          "end": 172.44299999999998,
          "en": "to the concrete data encoded in the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.47,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "Now, why is this helpful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 178.03,
          "en": "Well, we could, for example use this now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.03,
          "end": 182.32,
          "en": "to get our newsId like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.32,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "and then if we had a database, if we had some backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 189.28,
          "en": "from which we can fetch our news",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.28,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "we could send a request to the backend API here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.56,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "to fetch the news item with newsId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 203.05,
          "en": "That's what we could do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.05,
          "end": 204.72,
          "en": "I will not do it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.72,
          "end": 208.38,
          "en": "because we'll soon dive into data fetching and data storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.38,
          "end": 211.65,
          "en": "and we'll see different approaches we can use there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.65,
          "end": 214.87,
          "en": "with Next.js so we are going to take a look at that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.87,
          "end": 216.88,
          "en": "in detail in a couple of minutes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.88,
          "end": 221.142,
          "en": "but we could do this here if we had such a backend API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.142,
          "end": 222.18,
          "en": "but we don't have it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.18,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "because that's just a simple dummy app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 227.17000000000002,
          "en": "to get started with the file based routing system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.17000000000002,
          "end": 229.14,
          "en": "but that is how it would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.14,
          "end": 231.47,
          "en": "And that's how we can build dynamic pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.47,
          "end": 233.97,
          "en": "which work for different pieces of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.97,
          "end": 236.31,
          "en": "and then can do different things based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.31,
          "end": 238.48,
          "en": "on different pieces of data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.48,
          "end": 242.1,
          "en": "Here, we could fetch different news items from a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 245.963,
          "en": "based on the different Ids for which we visit this page.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
